# Netlify URL rewriting for clean product URLs
#
# Format: /<clean-url>  /<actual-file>?<params>  <status>
#   Status 200 = rewrite (browser keeps showing the clean URL)
#   Status 301 = permanent redirect (browser shows new URL — don't use here)
#
# This lets customers visit /wedding-invitations and see "/wedding-invitations"
# in their address bar, while the server quietly serves upload-and-print.html
# with ?product=wedding-invitations.
#
# To add a new product type:
#   1. Add a cost spec for it in admin (e.g., productType "Save the Dates"), publish
#   2. Add a line below mapping the slug to the configurator
#      Example:  /save-the-dates  /upload-and-print.html?product=save-the-dates  200
#   3. Optionally add a card to products.html linking to the clean URL
#
# Slug rule: lowercase the product name, replace spaces with hyphens.
# "Save the Dates" → save-the-dates, "Order of Service" → order-of-service.

/wedding-invitations  /upload-and-print.html?product=wedding-invitations  200
/save-the-dates       /upload-and-print.html?product=save-the-dates       200
